Firstmate fork: ChatGPT consultation channel
============================================

Ported from the fork's earlier core-edit implementation (origin/main
bin/fm-chatgpt-*.sh) into the fork layer without behaviour changes except
those listed under "Differences from the core-edit version". Like fork/README,
this file is plain text with no extension so upstream's documentation-audience
check does not require it in an upstream-owned inventory.

Firstmate asks ChatGPT to write a worker audit prompt and an execution plan,
and hands each one to an ordinary worker. ChatGPT is reached through the
already-installed codex-chatgpt-web bridge on loopback; this is a
consultation channel, not a Pi provider, and never executes local tools.


Files
-----

  fm-chatgpt-bridge-lib.sh  bridge URL resolution (loopback only), model slug,
                            Codex turn stamping, bounded health probe.
  fm-chatgpt-consult.sh     one self-contained Responses turn per call; prints
                            the answer, or fails with the bridge's diagnostic.
  fm-chatgpt-loop.sh        per-task state machine, prompt building, worker
                            dispatch and handoff, bridge start/stop.
  audit-brief-template      injected verbatim into audit-stage instructions;
                            the single owner of the generated audit prompt's
                            shape. A missing template refuses the consult.

Each script's header owns its exact rules; fm-chatgpt-loop.sh --help lists the
commands. Tests: fork/tests/fm-fork-chatgpt-*.test.sh.


Running a loop
--------------

  L=<task id>
  fork/chatgpt/fm-chatgpt-loop.sh init --task $L --objective-file F [--context-file F]
  fork/chatgpt/fm-chatgpt-loop.sh consult --stage audit --task $L
  fork/chatgpt/fm-chatgpt-loop.sh dispatch --stage audit --task $L -- $L <project> --mode M --yolo Y
  fork/chatgpt/fm-chatgpt-loop.sh record-findings --task $L       (after the audit worker reports)
  fork/chatgpt/fm-chatgpt-loop.sh consult --stage plan --task $L
  fork/chatgpt/fm-chatgpt-loop.sh dispatch --stage plan --task $L -- $L <project> --mode M --yolo Y
  fork/chatgpt/fm-chatgpt-loop.sh record-result --task $L --file F

State lives in data/<L>/chatgpt-loop.json. The arguments after -- are
fm-spawn.sh arguments and must start with the worker's plain task id. Run
with FM_HOME set to the home the worker belongs to.


Bridge
------

CHATGPT_WEB_BRIDGE_URL overrides the default http://127.0.0.1:17841/v1;
non-loopback values are refused. Installation and authentication stay
external. "fm-chatgpt-loop.sh bridge start|stop" operates only the daemon
under ~/tools/codex-chatgpt-web and never a process it did not start.
config/chatgpt-consultation (gitignored) is created on a consult attempt and
marks the home as using the channel, so a dead bridge reads "unreachable"
rather than "unconfigured".

Health check, at intake whenever the task's preferred flow is this channel:

  bash -c '. fork/chatgpt/fm-chatgpt-bridge-lib.sh && fm_chatgpt_bridge_health'

  healthy        a bounded test turn completed; consult.
  unconfigured   nothing listening, home never used the channel.
  unreachable    nothing listening, home uses the channel.
  unhealthy      listening, but the test turn failed.
  misconfigured  CHATGPT_WEB_BRIDGE_URL was refused.

When the preferred flow cannot run (unreachable, unhealthy, misconfigured),
report it to the captain - what is wrong, and whether to start the bridge or
proceed without consultation under a recorded local waiver - instead of
quietly dispatching without it.


Consult gate
------------

The fork's consult-gate policy (fork/bin/fm-launch-policy, enabled by
config/fork-policies) is separate from this channel and judges every ship or
scout launch by data/<launched id>/ only. With it enabled:

  - Fresh dispatch. The worker passes only through its OWN
    data/<id>/chatgpt-loop.json, so the worker task id must be the loop's
    task id L, dispatched while the loop is at the stage's dispatch phase.
    A worker with any other id is refused at spawn; the loop records the
    spawn failure and stays at <stage>-dispatch. Distinct worker ids need a
    gate change (deferred; see docs/M2.txt V11).
  - The plan stage under the gate also needs worker id L, so the audit
    worker L must be finished and cleaned up before the plan dispatch. How
    fm-spawn treats a second fresh launch of a still-recorded task id is not
    covered by the fork tests.
  - Relaunch. After fm-send confirms the handoff, dispatch writes
    data/<worker>/fork-consult-delivered.json as {"stage": "audit"|"plan"},
    the relaunch delivery proof the policy accepts. A new dispatch removes any
    earlier proof before spawning, a failed spawn or handoff writes none, and
    next-round removes the finished round's proof. Nothing is written to the
    worker's upstream state/<id>.meta.
  - A launch that must proceed without consultation needs a local waiver,
    data/<id>/fork-consult-waiver.json (see fork/README).

With the gate disabled the loop works exactly as above with any worker id;
the proof file is still written but nothing requires it.


Differences from the core-edit version
--------------------------------------

  - Delivery proof is data/<worker>/fork-consult-delivered.json, not a
    consult_delivered= line in state/<worker>.meta.
  - The spawn no longer carries FM_CHATGPT_LOOP_DISPATCH_TASK; only the old
    core gate read it, and the fork gate does not.
  - Not ported: the core consult gate (bin/fm-consult-gate-lib.sh) and
    fm-spawn --consult-waived; the CHATGPT_BRIDGE startup health line
    (a bin/fm-bootstrap.sh / bin/fm-startup-network.sh edit); the
    chatgpt-consultation and audit-brief agent skills, which would need
    upstream-owned .agents/skills/ paths. Run the health check above by hand;
    a fork-owned startup line could later use an existing extension point
    (a registered check, bin/fm-check-register.sh) without core edits.
